       If exactly one, record the direction: if colors[v] == nxt_t(colors[u]), then u -> v (u parent of v).
       If the other, v -> u.
   If all edges have a direction, we now have a directed graph.
   Check if this directed graph is a valid rooted tree:
       - Compute in-degree of each node (number of edges directed towards it).
       - There must be exactly one node with in-degree 0 (the root).
       - All other nodes must have in-degree exactly 1.
       - The underlying undirected graph is connected (it is, since original is tree and we directed all edges).
       - The root must have out-degree <= 2 (which is equivalent to undirected degree <= 2, since in-degree=0).
   If valid, let r be the root. Check if colors[r] matches the start color of type t (i.e., colors_order[t][0]). If yes, return r.
   (Note: if the root's color doesn't match t's start, could there be a valid root with a different type? We are iterating all t, so we'll catch it in another t.)

